From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: sc8280xp: suspend the card and its streams

The card sets no PM ops, and qcom_snd_parse_of() marks every DPCM link
ignore_suspend, so snd_soc_suspend() never runs for it and open PCMs are
never suspended. Wire up snd_soc_pm_ops and clear ignore_suspend on this
card's links; none of them has to run while the system sleeps.

Ported from Armada: https://github.com/armada-os/armada/blob/410bcf26a67f3e5d38e487d0ec84c5632f2bc3f6/packages/kernel/patches/0528-ASoC-qcom-sc8280xp-suspend-the-card-and-its-streams.patch
---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
@@ -185,6 +185,9 @@
 			link->be_hw_params_fixup = sc8280xp_be_hw_params_fixup;
 			link->ops = &sc8280xp_be_ops;
 		}
+
+		/* Nothing on these cards has to play across system suspend */
+		link->ignore_suspend = 0;
 	}
 }
 
@@ -245,6 +248,7 @@
 	.driver = {
 		.name = "snd-sc8280xp",
 		.of_match_table = snd_sc8280xp_dt_match,
+		.pm = &snd_soc_pm_ops,
 	},
 };
 module_platform_driver(snd_sc8280xp_driver);
